messages:
talia_sales: Mount & Co wants a 4-day POC: streaming websocket with function-calls, NDJSON structured output, webhook HMAC + replay nonce. They asked for Dedicated pricing and a security Q&A by Wed. Can eng/security scope blockers?

ben_se: Clarify p95 SLA and whether ordering is required. Also will they accept HMAC or insist on mTLS?

talia_sales: p50 < 80ms, p95 < 350ms. Ordering preferred but idempotency ok. They prefer HMAC for POC.

ravi_security: For POC we recommend HMAC with rotating keys, KMS for key storage, org retention=7 days, and SOC2 evidence. We'll draft answers.

ben_se: Implementation plan: websocket stream emits 'invoke' events with call_id; client POSTs to webhook with X-Mountco-HMAC and X-Call-Id. Sample runbook snippet:

```
ws.on('message', m => {
  const e = JSON.parse(m);
  if (e.type==='invoke') fetch(webhook, {method:'POST', headers:{'X-Mountco-HMAC':sign(e.payload),'X-Call-Id':e.id}, body:JSON.stringify(e.payload)}).then(()=>ws.send(JSON.stringify({id:e.id,status:'ok'})));
});
```

ben_se: For 5k QPS we'll recommend Dedicated sizing; I'll add cost ballpark.

ops-bot: config change queued: set retention_days=7 for org=mountco-poc. ETA 2026-06-01T05:00:00Z.

talia_sales: Timeline: security answers by Wed EOD, runbook by Thu AM, pricing by Thu EOD. Posting webhook + questionnaire when received. Thx!
